course: dictionary
lesson: 6432
title: Mysteriously
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Mysteriously» is an adverb. It tells you how something happens. It means in a strange way that cannot be explained, so if something mysteriously vanishes, nobody knows how or why it went.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The light mysteriously went out» tells you the light went off, but not in an ordinary way. The clue is the strange event, and the -ly ending shows that the word describes how the action happens.
explain: Writers use this word to make readers curious. «The key mysteriously disappeared» makes you want to find out why. A second meaning is about secrets: «she smiled mysteriously» means she was keeping something hidden on purpose.
fact: Mysteriously is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens.
fact: «Mysteriously» means in a way that is strange and cannot be explained.
fact: «Mysteriously» can also mean in a secretive way, keeping something hidden on purpose, as in «she smiled mysteriously».
fact: Common phrases with this word are «mysteriously disappeared» and «mysteriously vanished».
fact: The comparative form is «more mysteriously», used when you compare how two things happen.
exercise: «The light mysteriously went out.» What does mysteriously tell us about how the light went out? | Very quickly, like a switch | *In a strange way nobody can explain | In a happy way | With a loud bang
exercise: «She smiled mysteriously and said nothing.» What does mysteriously suggest? | She was very cold | *She was keeping a secret on purpose | She was about to sneeze | She was singing loudly
exercise: «The key mysteriously disappeared from the drawer.» Find and copy the adverb. | *mysteriously | disappeared | drawer | key
test: «The door opened in the night.» Which word fits the gap in the sentence «The door ___ opened in the night» to show it was strange? | loudly | happily | *mysteriously | slowly
test: «A duck's quack that mysteriously never echoes.» What does this tell the reader? | The duck is hungry and tired | The duck is lost in a park | *Something strange happens that nobody can explain | The duck quacks very loudly
exam: «She smiled mysteriously.» Which meaning fits best? | She was in a hurry | She was crying | *She was keeping something hidden on purpose | She was very tired
